+
+## Per-Profile Base System Prompt (Local Patch)
+
+The local `per-profile-system-prompt-v1` patch adds `system_prompt` to
+`OpenHandsAgentProfile` and `OpenHandsAgentSettings`. This is a local extension,
+not a feature of the unmodified 1.49.1 release.
+
+- `None` (JSON `null`) uses the SDK's built-in base prompt.
+- A string replaces that base prompt verbatim; it is not rendered as Jinja.
+- An empty string intentionally removes the static base prompt.
+
+```python
+from openhands.sdk.profiles import OpenHandsAgentProfile
+
+corpus = OpenHandsAgentProfile(
+    name="corpus",
+    llm_profile_ref="local-model",
+    system_prompt="Use the corpus tools and cite the retrieved sources.",
+    mcp_server_refs=["corpus"],
+)
+```
+
+Profile resolution passes this value to the existing `Agent(system_prompt=...)`
+constructor. Skills, runtime context and `system_message_suffix` remain separate
+parts of the initial system context. Existing conversations retain their saved
+agent and system prompt; profile edits affect newly created conversations.
+ACP profiles do not accept this field.
+
+The patched local Canvas editor exposes a checkbox and multiline text field.
+For a custom prompt, select the agent profile's configured LLM before starting a
+chat. Canvas rejects a conflicting selection rather than silently falling back
+to global agent settings and losing the custom prompt.
